<title>AUSTRALIA: Mayne shares up on government's Optus plan.</title>
<headline>Mayne shares up on government's Optus plan.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Mayne Nickless Ltd rose over two percent on Friday on hopes the government's plan to ease foreign shareholder restrictions on Optus Communications could pave the way for a quicker sale of Mayne's stake in Optus.</p>
<p>At 11.00 a.m. (0100 GMT) Mayne shares were 18 cents up or 2.24 percent at A$8.22 on light volume.</p>
</text>
